1
00:00:01,668 --> 00:00:03,586
As countries worldwide are battling

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:06,339
a discrete yet fierce information war,

3
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:08,967
Westalis launched "Operation Strix,"

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:12,887
in order to track the movements
of Ostania's key government officials.

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:15,849
B-1 Agent, Twilight,
is in charge of the operation.

6
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:18,393
He successfully completed Phase One,
by creating a family

7
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:22,397
and enrolling his daughter into
a prestigious school.

8
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:26,985
Currently, she managed to secure one of
the eight Stella Stars

9
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:29,612
that are necessary to become
an honor student.

10
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,448
The mission has now entered Phase Two,

11
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:37,412
which is to attend the reception where
the target, Desmond, will appear.

12
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:45,044
ORIGINAL WORK BY TATSUYA ENDO
SERIALIZED ON SHUEISHA'S SHONEN JUMP PLUS

13
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:15,927
MISSION 20:
INVESTIGATE THE GENERAL HOSPITAL

14
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:18,304
The social studies project this time,

15
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:21,015
is to research an occupation
that interests you.

16
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:24,227
You may ask your parents
about their workplace

17
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:27,522
or interview local shops and companies.

18
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:31,067
You may also have your parents arrange
an interview with prominent figures.

19
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:35,697
And of course, if you want to do research
about teachers, you may come to me.

20
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,700
I will lecture you on
the pride of an educator.

21
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:43,830
Prepare a report about your research
and present it to the class on Friday.

22
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:45,915
Damian, will you interview your father?

23
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:47,792
If I can reach him.

24
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:52,589
I'll get this done efficiently
by asking my dad about his company.

25
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:54,591
What about you, Anya?

26
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,305
Job research?

27
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,891
We were told to ask

28
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:06,311
why you chose the job,
and how we can work in that field.

29
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:09,188
And they told us to observe you at work.

30
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:11,816
What? My job?

31
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:15,320
What should I do?
She wants to observe me at work?

32
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:16,654
But which job?

33
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,532
Are you ready, Anya?

34
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:21,910
Let me tell you about my job.

35
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:22,827
Okay.

36
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:28,833
I first started this job
in order to support my younger brother,

37
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,002
but now I take pride in my work.

38
00:03:31,085 --> 00:03:32,962
Shopkeeper also told me

39
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:35,590
that this is a noble calling,
and I'm like a soldier

40
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:38,343
who devotes her life to her homeland.

41
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:41,846
Oh, it's a mission from the Shopkeeper.

42
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:45,475
This is my target.

43
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:48,186
He's a bastard traitor!

44
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:52,398
It seems like he's done horrible things
that I can't even mention to you, Anya.

45
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,611
Let's go see him.

46
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:58,863
-Can you keep up with me, Anya?
-Yes.

47
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:01,658
The Shop researches the target's

48
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:04,118
capabilities and layout of the security,

49
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:05,870
so I just have to get inside.

50
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:08,331
I must kill the enemy at first sight,

51
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:10,875
but killing the wrong person
is out of the question,

52
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,877
so I make sure to read the file carefully.

53
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:15,880
I approach boldly,
since I have nothing to be ashamed of.

54
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:17,715
There's danger!

55
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,759
This job is rewarding

56
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:23,137
because I know that I am
cleaning up this country.

57
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:27,600
When I think of all the lives that are
being protected because of my job,

58
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:29,394
it instills power into my weapon.

59
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:34,023
What this job requires is
training of the body and technique.

60
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:37,318
A good understanding of
human anatomy is helpful too.

61
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,279
The enemy is a human after all,

62
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:40,947
so I strive to kill them

63
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:44,659
quickly without causing too much pain.

64
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:51,874
For example, if you take
the knife on the neck, and cut it,

65
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:54,002
a human will die instantly.

66
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:58,715
Aside from that, a precise hit to
the vital parts of the brain and heart…

67
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,176
Oh no, are you okay, Anya? Let's tell Loid

68
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,680
that we went to the tomato festival!

69
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:11,102
Anya is thinking of doing research
on Father's job.

70
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:14,272
Is that right?
That sounds like a good idea!

71
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:16,441
A job at the City Hall is meaningful,

72
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:18,943
but it might be a little boring for you.

73
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,611
I'm back.

74
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:23,323
Father, this and that.

75
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,782
Okay. Roger.

76
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:26,743
TWO DAYS LATER
BERLINT GENERAL HOSPITAL

77
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:29,704
I work in the Psychiatric Department
of this hospital.

78
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:34,042
Everyone knows you're coming today,
but don't cause any trouble.

79
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:34,959
Okay.

80
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:37,754
It's huge.

81
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:40,465
It's the most prominent hospital
in the capital.

82
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:44,343
Being a private medical practitioner
would've been a better cover,

83
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:48,222
but key figures in the political, business
and military circles use this hospital.

84
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:50,099
So I can steal intel,

85
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,977
and it gives me the opportunity
to forge connections.

86
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,981
I haven't said anything for you
to take notes on.

87
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,942
And what's with that outfit?

88
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:03,488
-It's the classic investigation outfit.
-I see.

89
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:13,831
Psychiatrists don't usually
wear lab coats,

90
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:16,501
but this makes me look more
like a doctor, right?

91
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,504
What are you going to research?

92
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:24,509
The first question is,
why did you choose this job?

93
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:28,888
The reason why I chose this job?
Let's see.

94
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,767
Everyone catches a cold
and gets sick, right?

95
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,894
Sometimes your mind gets sick too.

96
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:39,649
There are many people in this world
whose mind catches a cold.

97
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:44,237
The second son told me that I'll never
catch a cold because I'm dumb.

98
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,156
I see. Try to get along with him.

99
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:49,075
Anyways,

100
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:52,078
I wanted to help those people out.

101
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:55,832
There are also many veterans
who are still suffering

102
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:58,167
even years after the war ended.

103
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:02,547
I figured that if Desmond
is secluding himself from society

104
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,674
because of some sickness,

105
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:08,219
then I could perhaps approach him
as a doctor…

106
00:07:08,886 --> 00:07:11,180
I made a firm resolve in college…

107
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:15,935
The next question is,
what's the work atmosphere like?

108
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:17,478
Atmosphere?

109
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,439
Hello, Doctor Forger.

110
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:22,567
Is this your daughter?

111
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:25,570
These are my colleagues. Say hello.

112
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:28,072
It's very nice to meet you.

113
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:29,991
You're so cute!

114
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:31,868
What a good girl, doing your homework!

115
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:34,745
She's so cute like a princess.

116
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:36,080
Here's a snack for you.

117
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:39,917
Father's workplace is like paradise.

118
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,169
Good for you.

119
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:44,547
How is my father at work?

120
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:47,425
He's so cool!

121
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:50,011
He's so attentive and kind
towards the patients too.

122
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:52,722
Your father is an amazing man.

123
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:56,184
He quickly became our leading force
soon after he transferred here.

124
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:59,562
But he's not arrogant,
and is loved by everyone.

125
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:02,899
By the way, my friend
in the Neurology Department said that

126
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:05,276
she wants Doctor Forger to attend
the next gathering…

127
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:07,153
The Director wants to go golfing with you.

128
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:08,946
Father, are you popular?

129
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:12,241
Well, I try to be sociable.

130
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,659
Can you tell the Director…

131
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:16,412
It's best to widen my network.

132
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:20,500
It makes it easier to gain intel
and connections, but most importantly,

133
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:24,921
a spy must make others think,
"No, there's no way he's a spy."

134
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,256
One must be sociable without standing out.

135
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,259
"No, there's no way he's a spy."

136
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:33,763
You keep on writing notes at weird times.

137
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:36,974
What's the most difficult part
about this job?

138
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:39,060
That's a good question.

139
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,394
Let's see.

140
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:44,148
It's the difficulty of working with
the mind, which is not visible.

141
00:08:44,815 --> 00:08:47,151
Doctors aren't wizards.

142
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:49,362
We can't read people's minds.

143
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:52,198
Why do you look so proud?

144
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:56,077
Because we can't read minds,
we must let go of all preconceptions,

145
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:59,372
and observe carefully and patiently,
and interact with them.

146
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:02,500
It's just like a spy
getting to know his target.

147
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:05,169
But one big difference is

148
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:08,130
a spy would betray that trust in the end…

149
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,007
These snacks are so good.

150
00:09:10,091 --> 00:09:12,218
Do you want some more?

151
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:14,929
-Do you want juice?
-Want to take a personality test?

152
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:16,389
I'm done answering questions.

153
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:18,391
Father is so serious.

154
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,685
That's his charm.

155
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:22,812
We wish you would use your talent

156
00:09:22,895 --> 00:09:24,897
and work at the clinic.

157
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:28,609
I'm sorry.
I'm so busy with my research studies.

158
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:30,403
I guess what's most difficult,

159
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:33,155
is the fact that I'm doing this
along with my mission.

160
00:09:33,739 --> 00:09:35,950
All right, we'll head back to work.

161
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,660
Bye Anya!

162
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:40,371
I was to see you actually working.

163
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:41,831
The consultations?

164
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:45,001
I can't let you do that since it concerns
the patient's privacy.

165
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:48,671
I can't let outsiders
near my research either.

166
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:53,175
I guess I can let you see
the consultation room.

167
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:56,429
I don't plan to use this room today.

168
00:09:56,512 --> 00:10:00,016
This is not like the operation room.
It looks like a normal room.

169
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,685
It's made this way to help
the patients relax.

170
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:06,230
Where's the brain reconstruction machine?

171
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:08,733
What do you think psychiatrists do?

172
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:12,445
Stop fooling around
and let's finish all of your questions.

173
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:14,697
What kind of anime is she
getting this from?

174
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:17,867
I'm pretty much finished now.
I'm a little bored now.

175
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,493
Don't touch anything!

176
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:21,203
Create a ruckus and I'll get mad.

177
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:23,039
Behind this bookshelf,

178
00:10:23,122 --> 00:10:26,334
is an emergency escape route
for my missions.

179
00:10:26,417 --> 00:10:28,210
It will move once the lever is pulled.

180
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,838
A hidden passage! Lever!

181
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:34,842
Oh, it's a WISE agent.

182
00:10:34,925 --> 00:10:37,136
Sorry, some urgent business came up.

183
00:10:37,219 --> 00:10:40,431
Since you're finished,
should I have Yor come pick you up?

184
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,685
I'll wait until your work is finished.

185
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:46,395
Being a spy is hard work.

186
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:47,855
Okay.

187
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:50,858
Then play with this while you wait.

188
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,361
I use these during consultations.

189
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:57,406
Arrange these figurines and other items
however you like inside this box.

190
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,783
It'll be fun.

191
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:00,201
Sounds boring.

192
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:03,496
Listen up. Don't touch anything else.

193
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,830
Okay.

194
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,749
I'll be back in ten minutes.

195
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:12,671
Huh.

196
00:11:16,675 --> 00:11:19,387
The materials for
the revised version of the DSM.

197
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:21,889
-They should arrive by this weekend.
-Thanks.

198
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,558
In order to keep my cover,

199
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:27,978
there are few agents working
within this hospital.

200
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:30,523
Another mission, huh.

201
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:33,734
-Did you work out my schedule here?
-Of course.

202
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:38,697
That child I saw earlier is Anya Forger?
She seems to be close to you.

203
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:41,242
She's unpredictable so it keeps me
on my toes.

204
00:11:41,325 --> 00:11:44,995
I'm surprised that she's able to
challenge you.

205
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:55,005
What an exciting adventure!

206
00:11:55,589 --> 00:11:58,259
The hidden passage is so narrow.

207
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:02,513
Today's topic is about
paranormal experience and neuroscience.

208
00:12:02,596 --> 00:12:04,390
Is it a serious meeting?

209
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:08,227
Of all the reported cases,
five percent are unexplainable…

210
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:10,271
This is absurd!

211
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:13,566
Those who talk about seeing ghosts
and what-not are mythomaniacs!

212
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:17,027
Or it could be illusions caused by
abnormal cerebral dysfunction.

213
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,196
There is no scientific proof.

214
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:22,032
Ghost stories? How exciting!

215
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,122
Did you hear something?

216
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:30,666
But there are no rooms above us.

217
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:33,294
Oh no! They'll find out about
the hidden passage.

218
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:36,297
You're just hearing things.

219
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:41,385
Anyway, if this topic comes up
when providing treatment,

220
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:43,387
we must be very careful--

221
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:46,807
It's a waste of time to even discuss it.
Let's end this meeting.

222
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:51,437
Anya has to go back soon,
or Father will return!

223
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:55,941
My foot is stuck, and I can't get it out!

224
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:58,944
Anya is in a crisis!

225
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:08,120
What is that? There's something up there!

226
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:09,497
It sounds like a baby's cry!

227
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,374
It's a ghost! It's got to be a ghost!

228
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:16,629
I got it out! I have to hurry back!

229
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,677
It went away.

230
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:27,473
I heard about a baby who haunts this
place because it died due to malpractice.

231
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:29,391
It was a true story!

232
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:32,311
Everyone, let's continue our meeting!

233
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:34,230
Yes, let's! From now on,

234
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:37,900
we must listen to clients
who speak about paranormal activities.

235
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:46,325
Let's see how she arranged everything
inside that box.

236
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:48,035
Father is coming back!

237
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:50,871
I have to hurry up and make something!

238
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:54,542
I'm back.

239
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:57,628
Playing with these figurines
is so much fun.

240
00:13:57,711 --> 00:14:00,381
Let's take a look. Believe it or not,

241
00:14:00,464 --> 00:14:04,134
this game reveals a bit of
a person's unconscious mind.

242
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:06,887
Let's see what's on your mind.

243
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:08,389
It's chaos!

244
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,141
What is this?

245
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:13,018
I've never seen a case like this!

246
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:14,853
I just threw everything in.

247
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:18,607
What's up with these figurines
that are scattered and buried?

248
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:20,651
They were all attacked

249
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:24,405
by the bad people's rolling sweep attack.

250
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:26,156
What is this?

251
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,534
I don't know what this means,
but it's a catastrophe!

252
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:31,245
I was so preoccupied
that I failed to realize

253
00:14:31,328 --> 00:14:34,748
that she was taken from
the orphanage to live with a stranger.

254
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,001
It's normal for her to experience stress.

255
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,044
No, Father, this is…

256
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:42,673
She must have been trying so hard
to suppress and hide her feelings.

257
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:46,343
I never knew that it had evolved into
this deep, dark abyss.

258
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:49,054
No, I was just pretending not to see it.

259
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:52,558
Yes, this is my weakness.
I have failed as a spy.

260
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:54,226
I must help her.

261
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:57,021
Let's go home for today.

262
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:59,899
Let's buy the latest Spy Wars book
at the bookstore.

263
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,442
Y… yay!

264
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:04,904
Let's write up the report together
after dinner.

265
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:07,698
-Did you take lots of notes?
-No, Father…

266
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,700
My notes about the spy…

267
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:13,203
What is this?!

268
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:15,164
I can't read her writing at all.

269
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:18,334
Um… this is…

270
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:22,129
Anya will work hard
and write the report on her own.

271
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:26,175
Is that right? Good girl! You're the best!

272
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,802
Mother, we're home!

273
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:30,804
Welcome home!

274
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:34,808
Were you able to see Loid's
super cool concussive therapy?

275
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:35,726
Concussive?

276
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:38,062
Um, Yor, that's only used
during emergencies.

277
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:40,689
He was throwing down patients
left and right.

278
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:42,316
It was a sight to see.

279
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:44,026
Father is violent.

280
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:46,278
Yor…

281
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:50,908
In the future,

282
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:54,411
I hope I can do the same kind of job.
The end.

283
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:59,541
That was a very heartfelt,
and elegant report.

284
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:03,671
Next is Anya Forger.

285
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:07,216
Father's job is a sp…

286
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:09,677
spectacular doctor who heals the mind.

287
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:13,138
In order to provide the patients
with peace of mind,

288
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:17,184
he works hard while sacrificing sleep
and taking digestive medicine.

289
00:16:17,851 --> 00:16:21,647
He said he wants to help people
who faced hardships during the war.

290
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:22,940
How lovely!

291
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:25,943
Just as I expected, Loid Forger.

292
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:29,238
In order to build trust with his targets,

293
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:31,865
he communicates with them
carefully and patiently.

294
00:16:31,949 --> 00:16:32,783
Target?

295
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:35,619
Father is frantically trying to
make connections.

296
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:39,289
During work, he plays golf
and has hidden secrets in his room.

297
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,542
He's also passing out snacks.

298
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:44,294
Snacks? Is that some code for bribery?

299
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:48,215
Also, he apparently punches
his patients sometimes.

300
00:16:48,298 --> 00:16:50,801
Loid Forger…

301
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,762
What's wrong, Twilight?

302
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:56,223
Nothing, I just got the chills.

303
00:16:56,306 --> 00:16:59,184
Later on, Loid was summoned to school,

304
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:02,438
but he was able to evade trouble
with his super eloquent skills.

305
00:17:03,939 --> 00:17:07,026
Top secret. A secret mission, huh?

306
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:09,903
A cipher?

307
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:11,071
SECRET CODE

308
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:13,657
Saturday. 8 a.m.

309
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:16,702
Meet me on the bridge.

310
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:19,163
MISSION 20: DECIPHER THE ARCANE CIPHERS

311
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:24,960
No wonder you're an elite member
of the organization.

312
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:26,670
You deciphered that so easily.

313
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:29,089
Anya's going to write a cipher too.

314
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:31,091
She's playing spy, huh.

315
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,473
-Anya.
-This is top secret!

316
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:42,394
Deciphering your code will be
the least of your problems.

317
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:47,858
Her writing

318
00:17:47,941 --> 00:17:51,111
is impossible to read
even with my deciphering skills.

319
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,362
Oh no.

320
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:54,656
I'm off to my night shift.

321
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,451
Make sure you study.

322
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:06,376
I love this scent of soap.

323
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,796
Mother, I have a favor to ask.

324
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:10,380
What is it, Anya?

325
00:18:10,964 --> 00:18:14,259
Can you write down something for me?

326
00:18:18,972 --> 00:18:22,392
SECRET CODE

327
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:25,813
The cipher is complete.

328
00:18:27,022 --> 00:18:29,608
Listen up. This is a secret mission.

329
00:18:29,691 --> 00:18:31,401
It's top secret.

330
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:35,572
Here's your mail.

331
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:38,784
Miss.

332
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,913
Put a stamp on the letter
and take it to the post office.

333
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:44,206
Oh no.

334
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:46,333
He rejected my cipher.

335
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:48,168
You can't do that, Anya.

336
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,422
-Right?
-That's so true.

337
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,719
Oh my. What is this?

338
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:02,141
What a strange letter. Is it a prank?

339
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:06,103
Come to think of it, my son was writing
something similar to this.

340
00:19:06,186 --> 00:19:08,605
He was copying some spy anime.

341
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,482
Oh, is that what it is?

342
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:13,652
That child is always pretending
to be a spy, isn't she?

343
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:18,532
Hey, what are you doing here?

344
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:21,201
-Scruffy.
-Is Loid home?

345
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:29,835
What? He's not home?
Fine then. I'll come back later.

346
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:31,044
Huh?

347
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:36,216
What is this? A message from Loid?

348
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:40,721
Tsk, tsk. It's top secret.

349
00:19:47,811 --> 00:19:49,563
Good morning, Anya.

350
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:55,277
What is this? A letter?

351
00:19:57,779 --> 00:19:59,489
It's not?

352
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:02,242
I got it.
It's the quiz that's popular these days!

353
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:05,746
It's top secret.

354
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:10,542
Come on Anya, tell me what it is!

355
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:14,004
Stop being mysterious
and tell me the answer!

356
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,053
Top secret!

357
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:23,013
Huh? What is this?

358
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:27,517
It's a cipher. Try to decipher it.

359
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:32,522
Why do I have to decipher this?

360
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:34,691
Do it yourself!

361
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:48,247
I'm excited to see who will come tomorrow!

362
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,794
You're amazing after all.

363
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,172
You were able to decipher that code.

364
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:05,222
Oh, this is the thing from yesterday.

365
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:10,560
What was this supposed to be?
It looks like a cipher.

366
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:13,355
This soft handwriting…

367
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:17,901
Was this written by a woman?
It smells good like soap!

368
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:23,115
Could this be a love letter?!

369
00:21:26,159 --> 00:21:29,830
Can you give this to him?
Keep it a secret.

370
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:33,458
This love is a top secret.

371
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:41,425
Saturday. 8 a.m.

372
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,969
Meet me on the bridge.

373
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:49,975
Don't underestimate the top informant
of the east and west.

374
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:54,229
Deciphering a simple code
is child's play to me!

375
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:57,607
But I was so excited that I couldn't
sleep a wink last night!

376
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:00,235
The morning sun is so bright!

377
00:22:00,944 --> 00:22:05,073
She used a secret code to meet me.
Where is this agent from?

378
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:08,076
Or is she a mystery lover?

379
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:11,788
"Decipher this love code
and come find me."

380
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:13,040
Is that what it means?

381
00:22:26,845 --> 00:22:28,972
It's top secret.

382
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:10,907
MISSION 21: NIGHTFALL
JEALOUSY FOR THE FIRST TIME

383
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:11,950
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
